.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-WAIT-FOR-IP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-wait-for-ip
.Nd wait up to thirty seconds for an IPv4 address other than loopback
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
returns as soon as the machine has an IPv4 address outside 127.0.0.0/8,
checking once a second, and gives up after thirty.
.Pp
It exists for
.Pa kldload-tls-cert.service ,
which runs it first: at first boot the certificate would otherwise be made
before DHCP has answered, naming no address a browser can reach.
Networking being
.Dq online
to systemd does not yet mean an address is bound.
.Pp
It exits 0 either way; the caller goes on regardless.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description at the top of the script and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, which had an address:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ time kldload-wait-for-ip

real	0m0.015s
user	0m0.005s
sys	0m0.007s
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
With a stand-in for
.Xr ip 8
that reports only loopback, and the wait cut to two seconds, the line it
prints when it gives up:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kldload-wait-for-ip: no IPv4 address after 30 s; going on without one
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "kldload-wait-for-ip: no IPv4 address after 30 s; going on without one"
The certificate made next will name no LAN address; it is made again when
one arrives.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr systemd.special 7 ,
.Xr ip 8 ,
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: it gave up without a word, and its test
could read
.Dq no address
while one was bound, when an early
.Xr grep 1
exit broke the pipe in front of it.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
IPv6 addresses do not count.
